[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3446111428","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112025#issuecomment-3446111428","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112025","id":3446111428,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NZ3zE","user":{"login":"BlueberryGecko","id":162060915,"node_id":"U_kgDOCajacw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/162060915?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko","html_url":"https://github.com/BlueberryGecko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-25T07:46:54Z","updated_at":"2025-10-26T21:50:31Z","body":"Note that the issue occurs no matter whether I pick the plant tile from terrain 0 or terrain 1, so I don't think the problem is that I just used a workflow that isn't supported. And since the result is consistently wrong in all these three cases, I'd guess that the algorithm just gives a wrong result.\n\n<img width=\"1400\" height=\"530\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/374b25d7-ab16-46f3-adab-ea0d9a156909\" />\n\nWhat actually confuses me in this screenshot is that the plant tile is present in **both** terrains, even though I defined its center bit as tileset 1. Maybe this gives a clue into the underlying issue?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3446111428/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3448235956","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112025#issuecomment-3448235956","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112025","id":3448235956,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Nh-e0","user":{"login":"IphStich","id":5625804,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MjU4MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5625804?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich","html_url":"https://github.com/IphStich","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-26T09:04:51Z","updated_at":"2025-10-26T09:04:51Z","body":"It appears to be the result of the constraints logic. Working on a PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3448235956/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3449303386","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112025#issuecomment-3449303386","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112025","id":3449303386,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NmDFa","user":{"login":"IphStich","id":5625804,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MjU4MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5625804?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich","html_url":"https://github.com/IphStich","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-27T02:51:17Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T02:51:17Z","body":"Turns out this isn't a bug, but is intentional (and poorly documented behaviour).\n\nThe peering bits aren't meant to describe the tile's **neighbours**, but rather what terrain exists **on the tile** itself at that side/corner.\n\nTiles in neighbouring cells join where the peering bits match each other along the side and corners.\n\nThe underlying idea is that one tile is meant to handle the transition between the different types of terrains, and to have the other one encroach on it. This is generally how tilesets are drawn, and it makes drawing the art easier while also meaning less work and less duplication. However, this does run counter to the intuition of terrain painting, where a person would view the cells as distinct blocks they are dropping the terrain into.\n\n---\n\nIn your project, the vine is encroaching on to the rock's tile, and takes up the bottom boundary of that tile. If you change the peering bits to accurately reflect that, as in the following example, then Godot behaves as expected.\n\n<img width=\"67\" height=\"295\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4781f8ed-b164-4f48-a5a0-9a2e083029f5\" />\n\nIf you really wanted to transition between different terrains at the border (instead of within one tile or the other) the best way to do this would be to create a new terrain which specifically describes the transitioning bits.\n\n<img width=\"67\" height=\"298\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19348ff2-9322-45e1-b25b-2abac0057d70\" />\n\nBoth of the above changes would solve the problem you're facing.\n\n---\n\nThis is ultimately not a bug because you have told Godot that \"at the **top** of this tile there is ground terrain\" and **not** \"use this tile if there is a ground tile **above** it\" (as we might suspect from intuition).\n\nThe reason the tile above changes to an up-down connecting one is because you are using the \"connect mode\" tool, and so Godot tries to find a pair of tiles that can connect the terrain between the the 2 cells. It finds the decoration 1 tile has ground at the top, so it assumed that you must have intended ground to connect the tiles, and swaps the tile in the above cell to one with ground at the bottom so that the peering bits can match.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3449303386/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3449389739","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112025#issuecomment-3449389739","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112025","id":3449389739,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NmYKr","user":{"login":"MadeScientist","id":190612698,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1yE2g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190612698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist","html_url":"https://github.com/MadeScientist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-27T03:46:51Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T03:59:34Z","body":"> Turns out this isn't a bug, but is intentional (and poorly documented behaviour).\n\nThanks for your detailed explanation, that is also helpful for me to know the autotiling work details. Can you open a new pr for documenting those 'feature' of autotiling? The doc poorly(in fact, none) records mechanics of how autotiling works, that will confuse user who using it in complex condition. Besides, sorry for suggesting   pr proposal at here.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3449389739/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3452841185","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112025#issuecomment-3452841185","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112025","id":3452841185,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Nzizh","user":{"login":"BlueberryGecko","id":162060915,"node_id":"U_kgDOCajacw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/162060915?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko","html_url":"https://github.com/BlueberryGecko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueberryGecko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-27T18:56:52Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T19:33:06Z","body":"Thank you so much for the explanation! I guess this makes some sense if we view it from an artist's instead of a programmer's perspective.\n\nI tested your suggested solution and it works, although I discovered another problem: \n\n<img width=\"647\" height=\"432\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f7cd32a9-ba02-4445-a6b1-76b3b2f678af\" />\n\nThe left tiles were painted using ground tiles first, then plant, and it correctly changes the ceiling tile.\n\nThe right tiles were painted with the plant first, then the ground tiles, which results in the wrong ceiling tile being picked. I assume the ceiling tile turned out wrong because the algorithm just picks the first tile with fitting rules (\"above me is a ground tile and I don't care what is below me\"), instead of going for the most _specific_ fit (\"above me is a ground tile _and_ below is a plant tile), which doesn't make sense in a constraint-based system -- unless of course, there's a specific reason for this.\n\n@IphStich are you in the mood of looking into this? Otherwise I'll open a separate issue for clarity. And thank you for your help :) \n\nRegarding this issue here, I can probably spend some time on the upcoming weekend to improve the documentation.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3452841185/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3453059499","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112025#issuecomment-3453059499","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112025","id":3453059499,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7N0YGr","user":{"login":"IphStich","id":5625804,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MjU4MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5625804?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich","html_url":"https://github.com/IphStich","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IphStich/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-27T19:54:24Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T19:54:24Z","body":"@BlueberryGecko don't bother with a new issue. The current algorithm isn't very good at respecting existing constraints, and there are other issues that describe different aspects of this same thing.\n\nI plan on looking into it and posting some PRs to help improve things. If you'd like, you can leave this issue open and I'll post updates here.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3453059499/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3479119443","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112025#issuecomment-3479119443","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112025","id":3479119443,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7PXyZT","user":{"login":"GameCarpenter","id":60531721,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTMxNzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60531721?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GameCarpenter","html_url":"https://github.com/GameCarpenter","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GameCarpenter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GameCarpenter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GameCarpenter/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GameCarpenter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GameCarpenter/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GameCarpenter/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GameCarpenter/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GameCarpenter/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GameCarpenter/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-03T06:41:41Z","updated_at":"2025-11-03T06:41:41Z","body":"I've come across a very similar issue. In my case, I was adding a second terrain that needed to be aware of the location of the ground/wall for orientation purposes. If feasible, a flag to change where you are peering to the tile center rather than the adjacent edge would be helpful in cases such as this one. Though having some understanding for what the center tile is meant to be used for otherwise would be useful.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3479119443/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]